 "hook": {
  "text": "WAS HE\nTHEIR KING?",
  "until": 3.0,
  "y": 0.12,
  "size": 120,
  "accent": [
   "KING?"
  ]
 },
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Archaeologists named him the Priest-King.",
   "emph": [
    "priest-king."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "There's just one problem.",
   "emph": [
    "problem."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Nothing says he was a priest... or a king.",
   "emph": [
    "priest...",
    "king."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Other ancient civilisations made sure you knew who was boss.",
   "emph": [
    "boss."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Egypt built pyramids for its pharaohs.",
   "emph": [
    "pyramids"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In Iraq, royals were buried in gold.",
   "emph": [
    "gold."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But the Indus people spread over more land than both of them combined.",
   "emph": [
    "indus",
    "combined."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And we haven't found one palace. No royal tomb. No statue of a conqueror. Not even a picture of a battle.",
   "emph": []
  },
  {
   "text": "Yet someone was clearly in charge.",
   "emph": [
    "someone"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In cities hundreds of kilometres apart, the bricks were made the same shape. One, two, four.",
   "caption": "In cities hundreds of kilometres apart, the bricks were made the same shape. 1, 2, 4.",
   "emph": [
    "same",
    "shape."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So who gave the orders? Rich merchants? Priests? A council? Archaeologists still argue.",
   "emph": []
  },
  {
   "text": "A giant civilisation... with no face of a ruler.",
   "emph": [
    "no",
    "face"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But one face is everywhere. On nearly seven of every ten seals... a creature no one else in the ancient world was carving.",
   "caption": "But one face is everywhere. On nearly 7 of every 10 seals... a creature no one else in the ancient world was carving.",
   "emph": [
    "everywhere.",
    "7",
    "10"
   ]
  }
 ],
